WEBVTT

00:02.394 --> 00:04.728
         ♪<i> It seems today</i>
        <i> that all you see</i> ♪

00:04.730 --> 00:07.840
     ♪<i> Is violence in movies</i>
         <i> and sex on TV</i> ♪

00:07.916 --> 00:11.493
      ♪<i> But where are those</i>
   <i> good old-fashioned values</i> ♪

00:11.570 --> 00:14.496
  ♪<i> On which we used to rely?</i> ♪

00:14.573 --> 00:18.166
 ♪<i> Lucky there's a family guy</i> ♪

00:18.244 --> 00:21.353
      ♪<i> Lucky there's a man</i>
     <i> who positively can do</i> ♪

00:21.430 --> 00:22.913
♪<i> All the things that make us</i> ♪

00:22.915 --> 00:23.856
        ♪<i> Laugh and cry</i> ♪

00:24.025 --> 00:30.195
          ♪<i> He's... a...</i>
       <i> Fam... ily... Guy!</i> ♪

00:30.847 --> 00:33.615
               ♪

00:35.594 --> 00:37.261
      New shirt, Cleveland?

00:37.263 --> 00:39.763
    Donna saw an unflattering
    picture of me on Facebook

00:39.765 --> 00:42.190
and only lets me wear black now.

00:42.268 --> 00:43.617
    Is the picture that bad?

00:43.693 --> 00:45.377
     It was the worst thing

00:45.454 --> 00:47.604
        I would ever want
        to see myself be.

00:47.606 --> 00:50.774
  Problem with these dark shirts
      is the dandruff shows.

00:50.776 --> 00:52.442
 But when I wear light colors...

00:52.444 --> 00:54.778
  The dandruff doesn't show, but
  you look bigger in the shirt.

00:54.780 --> 00:57.056
        -Yeah, it's called
      "Guillermo's Paradox."
        -What's that now?

00:57.132 --> 00:59.558
   Guillermo del Toro theorized
      that a fat man's shirt

00:59.635 --> 01:02.561
   cannot simultaneously appear
       slimming and clean.

01:02.638 --> 01:05.822
     Mm. That boy does look
     like he be gettin' dry.

01:05.824 --> 01:07.215
        All right, Peter,
        what's going on?

01:07.293 --> 01:08.400
      Well, truth be told,

01:08.477 --> 01:10.460
     Meg wants me to give her
         a bunch of money

01:10.462 --> 01:12.387
    so she can go to college,
          and I guess...

01:12.464 --> 01:15.056
     I guess I'd rather spend
      that money on alcohol.

01:15.134 --> 01:17.317
         Listen, I helped
   my daughter through college

01:17.394 --> 01:19.394
    and it was the best thing
           I ever did.

01:19.471 --> 01:21.655
        Well, it was just
 kind of us talking, but how so?

01:21.657 --> 01:24.750
    Right after she graduated,
     she got a real good job

01:24.827 --> 01:26.660
    and bought me a new car.

01:26.736 --> 01:28.754
     Says she's gonna buy me
         a house one day,

01:28.831 --> 01:31.590
     so I can sell this place
           and retire.

01:31.667 --> 01:34.927
      Man, imagine how great
   it would feel to be retired?

01:35.003 --> 01:36.837
       I knew a retired kid
         in high school.

01:36.913 --> 01:38.488
   All he ate was Tater Tots.

01:38.490 --> 01:41.325
       He smooshed a turtle
    like a ice cream sandwich.

01:41.327 --> 01:43.751
    -He was severely retired.
          -Okay, Peter.

01:43.829 --> 01:46.330
  Guys, I've got to help Meg get
       into a good college.

01:46.332 --> 01:49.333
Then I can have the golden years
    I've always dreamed of.

01:49.335 --> 01:51.668
 I sure am gonna miss you, baby.

01:51.670 --> 01:54.738
       New wife that's just
        one giant freckle?

01:57.767 --> 02:00.661
    Come on, Florida, cancer,
            let's go!

02:02.606 --> 02:04.606
         (Brian barking)

02:04.608 --> 02:06.291
   What's going on? You okay?

02:06.368 --> 02:08.852
   This-this squirrel, man...

02:08.854 --> 02:10.963
      (squirrel chittering)

02:11.039 --> 02:12.689
       Yeah, come down here
         and do it, huh?

02:12.691 --> 02:13.857
         Come down here!

02:13.859 --> 02:15.375
 Well, you're getting old, Bri.

02:15.452 --> 02:16.618
   Might be time to pack it up

02:16.695 --> 02:18.286
           and get out
  of the squirrel gettin' game.

02:18.364 --> 02:20.472
     No way, man. That little
    bastard comes down here...

02:20.549 --> 02:21.865
              Hey.

02:21.867 --> 02:24.125
          (chittering)

02:24.127 --> 02:26.052
          Get him, boy.

02:26.129 --> 02:28.480
               -♪
         -(Brian barking)

02:30.876 --> 02:32.876
            (panting)

02:32.878 --> 02:35.237
            (retches)

02:39.218 --> 02:41.218
You've got to get in shape, man.

02:41.220 --> 02:42.810
            You know,
   you should meet my trainer.

02:42.888 --> 02:44.221
 I think you'd really like him.

02:44.223 --> 02:45.330
       -You have a trainer?
              -Yes.

02:45.407 --> 02:47.574
       You think it's easy
    looking zero for 20 years?

02:47.651 --> 02:49.484
         All right, fine,
       I'll give it a shot.

02:49.561 --> 02:51.670
  Right now I feel more useless
       than a chiropractor

02:51.672 --> 02:53.321
        in an emergency.

02:53.399 --> 02:55.565
            Excuse me,
     is anyone here a doctor?

02:55.567 --> 02:57.234
       I have a heating pad
          in my office.

02:57.236 --> 02:58.902
  What seems to be the problem?

02:58.904 --> 03:01.329
           (cheering)

03:01.331 --> 03:03.164
               ♪

03:04.167 --> 03:06.259
         All right, Meg,
    now if we're gonna get you

03:06.336 --> 03:07.835
       into a good school,
         we're gonna have

03:07.913 --> 03:09.188
to fudge your application a bit.

03:09.264 --> 03:10.764
    Okay, how do we do that?

03:10.840 --> 03:12.249
 I don't know, I ate the fudge.

03:12.251 --> 03:13.583
      But the good news is

03:13.585 --> 03:15.360
I got a letter of recommendation
            for you.

03:15.362 --> 03:17.604
        It's from Big Bird
         and I wrote it.

03:17.681 --> 03:19.589
      -"When I first met..."
  -Read it as Big Bird, please.

03:19.591 --> 03:21.683
            (nasally):
     "When I first met Peter,

03:21.760 --> 03:24.428
   I was impressed at how tall
       and handsome he is."

03:24.430 --> 03:26.854
  That's coming from Big Bird?

03:26.932 --> 03:28.540
   Think of all the celebrities
            he's met.

03:28.617 --> 03:31.268
        Ryan Reynolds was
        on <i> Sesame Street.</i>

03:31.270 --> 03:34.104
              -Wow.
  -"Also, have you ever noticed

03:34.106 --> 03:36.456
           "that Grover
    and Super Grover are never

03:36.533 --> 03:38.792
         in the same room
        at the same time?"

03:38.868 --> 03:42.221
        As I said, Lois,
        not two days ago.

03:42.297 --> 03:44.056
               ♪

03:45.059 --> 03:47.117
       Principal Shepherd,
       what's it gonna take

03:47.119 --> 03:48.785
   to get Meg into a college?

03:48.787 --> 03:50.545
  If Meg has any chance at all,

03:50.622 --> 03:52.397
       she's going to need
      a little "extra help."

03:52.474 --> 03:54.399
       We'll do anything.
       Whatever it takes.

03:54.476 --> 03:58.528
         Good. Now you<i> do</i>
    understand how this works?

03:59.631 --> 04:01.073
         We understand.

04:01.149 --> 04:04.076
        I guess I'll, uh,
    I'll meet you in the car.

04:04.078 --> 04:06.227
     He didn't mean you have
        to sleep with him.

04:06.305 --> 04:08.730
    There are a few options.

04:08.732 --> 04:10.666
               ♪

04:12.736 --> 04:14.211
        (lights buzzing)

04:15.905 --> 04:18.648
    Now, Mr. And Mrs. Griffin,
          every college

04:18.650 --> 04:21.242
       has spots set aside
      for athletic recruits.

04:21.320 --> 04:22.928
      We can make Meg look
      like a star athlete.

04:23.005 --> 04:24.096
   With the click of a button,

04:24.490 --> 04:27.340
    we can make Meg look like
   she played varsity lacrosse,

04:27.417 --> 04:29.509
     won the Quahog Marathon,
         or had her head

04:29.511 --> 04:31.770
        roll down a temple
          in<i> Apocalypto.</i>

04:31.847 --> 04:33.330
               ♪

04:33.332 --> 04:35.256
     Lois, this is amazing!

04:35.334 --> 04:36.850
Meg's gonna look more successful

04:36.852 --> 04:38.944
        than a businessman
          in a hard hat.

04:38.946 --> 04:42.022
  Hey! I came down here from the
  office to point at the plans,

04:42.098 --> 04:44.724
      then at the building!
         Plans! Building!

04:44.726 --> 04:46.601
        Building! Plans!

04:46.603 --> 04:48.436
   Yes, sir. Right away, sir!

04:48.530 --> 04:50.622
         MAN (singing):

04:50.699 --> 04:53.700
     I come down to the site
         once in a while.

04:53.777 --> 04:56.295
               ♪

04:57.372 --> 04:59.673
       Hi, uh, you must be
        Stewie's trainer.

05:01.527 --> 05:04.361
 Wh... How did you...? I thought
 I was gonna meet your trainer?

05:04.363 --> 05:06.305
   You're looking at him, Bri.
         Look at my body.

05:06.381 --> 05:08.365
           I'm jacked.
     You want to get jacked?

05:08.367 --> 05:10.383
              -Uh...
  -Yeah, you want to get jacked.

05:10.385 --> 05:12.311
That's what having a trainer is.

05:12.387 --> 05:13.645
      Just a couple of guys
         getting jacked.

05:13.647 --> 05:15.705
     -Sometimes twice a day.
     -Okay, you know what...?

05:15.707 --> 05:18.317
  All right, before we start in,
  a little business to go over.

05:18.393 --> 05:20.819
 I was just messing around about
  the jacked stuff, by the way.

05:20.896 --> 05:23.213
   Uh, did you want to sign up
    for the full three years?

05:23.215 --> 05:25.324
   Three years? Don't you just
      do it by the session?

05:25.400 --> 05:27.701
       Yeah, no, we can do,
        uh, sesh to sesh.

05:27.736 --> 05:29.886
         Not committed.

05:29.888 --> 05:31.738
        Did you want to do
       the supplement plan?

05:31.856 --> 05:33.223
     Uh. uh, no. No, thanks.

05:33.225 --> 05:35.225
   Going through the motions.

05:35.227 --> 05:37.819
    All right, so what do you
   got going on for New Years?

05:37.896 --> 05:40.188
              -What?
    -80% of being a trainer is

05:40.265 --> 05:41.656
       asking clients what
   they're doing for New Years.

05:41.733 --> 05:44.234
 And then not seeming interested
        when you tell me.

05:44.236 --> 05:46.086
     I don't know, I might go
     over to a buddy's house

05:46.162 --> 05:47.587
    and watch the ball drop.

05:47.664 --> 05:49.422
          Oh, right on.

05:49.499 --> 05:51.257
     -So, uh, what do you do
            for work?
          -I'm a writer.

05:51.334 --> 05:53.259
    -Okay, so lot of sittin'?
              -Yeah.

05:53.336 --> 05:55.261
 Hang on, I got to make a call.

05:55.263 --> 05:58.582
   Hey, Death? I got a guy here
    just about ready for you.

05:58.584 --> 06:00.934
        No, not really,
I'm just trying to make a point.

06:00.936 --> 06:03.103
            All right,
    and that is it for today.

06:03.179 --> 06:04.863
    First sesh in the books.

06:04.865 --> 06:07.515
     Let's Ven' to the 'mo.

06:07.593 --> 06:09.493
               ♪

06:11.613 --> 06:15.690
            <i> CLEVELAND:</i>
     ♪<i> Mail time, mail time,</i>
      <i> mail time, mail time</i> ♪

06:15.767 --> 06:18.101
         ♪<i> Mail time.</i> ♪

06:18.103 --> 06:20.103
        The mail's here!

06:20.105 --> 06:22.214
        ♪<i> Here's the mail</i>
        <i> that never fails</i> ♪

06:22.290 --> 06:24.441
        ♪<i> It makes me want</i>
         <i> to wag my tail</i> ♪

06:24.443 --> 06:29.170
         ♪<i> When it comes</i>
     <i> I want to wail mail...</i> ♪

06:29.205 --> 06:30.872
        "To Meg Griffin."

06:30.949 --> 06:32.682
             (gasps)
         It's from Brown!

06:35.454 --> 06:37.879
             (gasps)
       I've been accepted!

06:37.956 --> 06:39.398
     Hey, that's great news.

06:39.474 --> 06:41.641
         Let's clap it up
    my high school girlfriend

06:41.718 --> 06:44.528
         and I still say
      I love you in e-mails.

06:46.573 --> 06:48.740
    I was hoping the good news
         and the clapping

06:48.817 --> 06:50.650
    would offset this secret.

06:50.727 --> 06:52.202
          But yay, Meg!

06:56.733 --> 06:58.625
               ♪

07:13.325 --> 07:16.176
 Wow, I remember when my parents
       clapped their hands

07:16.252 --> 07:18.161
after moving something one time.

07:18.163 --> 07:19.921
 You never forget those moments.

07:19.998 --> 07:22.499
  Now remember, Meg, I want you
      to call us every week,

07:22.501 --> 07:25.168
    and then every few weeks,
         and then never.

07:25.170 --> 07:26.519
         I promise, Mom.

07:26.521 --> 07:28.429
    Got to admit, I'm kind of
      jealous you get to go

07:28.431 --> 07:30.431
            to college
  and live in such a cool dorm.

07:30.433 --> 07:32.451
    Look, they even have the
    pay phone Denise Huxtable

07:32.527 --> 07:34.602
         would call from
      on<i> A Different World.</i>

07:34.604 --> 07:36.529
   Hi, Dad. College is great.

07:36.531 --> 07:38.623
      I'm doing what I want
           to actresses

07:38.625 --> 07:41.626
      and will get support
      from my wife Camille.

07:41.628 --> 07:44.629
     That stuff was more out
   in the open than I remember.

07:44.706 --> 07:46.631
      (indistinct chatter)

07:46.708 --> 07:48.467
    Well, I guess that's it.

07:48.543 --> 07:51.194
     Our baby is all grown up
      and living at college.

07:51.196 --> 07:52.712
     I know! She's so lucky!

07:52.714 --> 07:54.288
     This place is awesome!

07:54.366 --> 07:56.533
        You think I'll go
       to college one day?

07:56.535 --> 07:58.218
           Oh... yeah.

07:58.294 --> 07:59.478
     Sky's the limit, champ.

07:59.596 --> 08:01.128
     Lois, I'll meet you down
           at the car.

08:01.206 --> 08:02.722
       I got to take a dump
        that will live on

08:02.724 --> 08:05.358
       in story and song.

08:06.653 --> 08:08.302
  No, I don't have a roommate.

08:08.380 --> 08:10.063
        I guess he, like,
        died or something.

08:10.139 --> 08:12.306
       So I've got a double
          all to myself.

08:12.384 --> 08:14.159
     A double? Hey, roomie.

08:14.236 --> 08:16.386
   Want to listen to The Doors
     for the next six months

08:16.388 --> 08:18.221
       and then never again
    for the rest of your life?

08:18.223 --> 08:20.073
    Wait, you're my roommate?

08:20.149 --> 08:22.000
   You're Ashok Chandrasekhar?

08:22.077 --> 08:24.077
         -God bless you.
            -(laughs)

08:24.079 --> 08:26.487
         Classic Ashok.

08:26.565 --> 08:28.256
               ♪

08:29.510 --> 08:31.826
      Hey, why'd you tell me
    to meet you at Meg's room?

08:31.903 --> 08:33.419
      Well, now that Meg is
           in college,

08:33.496 --> 08:35.588
  I turned her room into a gym.

08:35.665 --> 08:37.599
           Oh, my God.

08:39.745 --> 08:42.187
       -How'd you do this?
      -Took a<i> Limitless</i> pill

08:42.264 --> 08:44.505
    and played "Old Town Road"
             on loop.

08:44.583 --> 08:46.525
     All right, why don't we
     start off with a plank?

08:46.601 --> 08:48.843
    One minute, and I'm gonna
      go call my girlfriend

08:48.920 --> 08:51.254
    and the forget about you.
            And... go.

08:51.256 --> 08:53.681
          -(phone beeps)
              -Hey.

08:53.759 --> 08:55.367
      -I'm at the gym, why?
             -Stewie?

08:55.443 --> 08:57.761
   Babe, you know I can't deal
        with your sister.

08:57.763 --> 09:00.446
  Hey, babe... babe? Baby girl?

09:00.523 --> 09:03.116
             -Stewie!
      -Babe! Babe, I'm not--
            baby babe,

09:03.192 --> 09:04.876
  ba-babe, baby, baby, come on.

09:04.953 --> 09:07.453
          -(sharp snap)
        -(shouts, moaning)
    -Babe, I'll call you back.

09:07.455 --> 09:09.122
            (moaning)

09:09.198 --> 09:11.383
      Okay, right on, so you
    remember I was telling you

09:11.459 --> 09:13.777
  about the magnesium supplement
       with the bone boost?

09:13.779 --> 09:16.279
     So this is why you want
      to try and take that.

09:16.281 --> 09:18.205
            -Right on?
       -No, not "right on"!

09:18.283 --> 09:19.391
 My arm feels like it's broken!

09:19.467 --> 09:21.451
  Oh, it's gonna need some P.T.

09:21.453 --> 09:23.228
    Let me give you the card
    of my physical therapist.

09:23.305 --> 09:24.621
         He's the best.

09:24.639 --> 09:27.065
       This is gonna be you
   in another shirt, isn't it?

09:27.142 --> 09:29.067
    Hey, what's the problemo?

09:29.069 --> 09:30.885
 Give me the rundown, go ahead.

09:30.962 --> 09:33.196
               ♪

09:34.633 --> 09:36.633
           H-Hey, Meg?

09:36.635 --> 09:38.076
         Hi, I'm Xander.

09:38.153 --> 09:39.803
    I'm-I'm in your bio class.
        I'm not a stalker.

09:39.805 --> 09:41.246
             (laughs)
           Either way.

09:41.397 --> 09:44.231
   Listen, me and my roommates
 are having people over tonight,

09:44.309 --> 09:46.585
       and I was wondering
    if you'd want to come by.

09:46.587 --> 09:48.253
       Yeah. I'd love to.

09:48.330 --> 09:49.087
            Awesome.

09:49.164 --> 09:51.238
          Keeney, 325.

09:51.316 --> 09:52.591
              PETER:
            Heads up!

09:52.667 --> 09:54.517
         (Meg exclaims)

09:54.519 --> 09:56.836
        Dad? What the hell
          are you doing?

09:56.913 --> 09:58.671
    I'm going to college now.

09:58.748 --> 10:00.265
   Wait, what? What about Mom?

10:00.342 --> 10:02.249
       Well, I had to have
       a tough conversation

10:02.327 --> 10:04.269
      with her by the lake.

10:04.346 --> 10:06.313
               ♪

10:10.335 --> 10:13.019
        I'm just not a fan
 of long-distance relationships.

10:13.096 --> 10:14.687
      Peter, I need to know
         if you're gonna

10:14.806 --> 10:16.263
   pick Stewie up from school.

10:16.341 --> 10:17.690
 I'll be home for Thanksgiving.

10:17.767 --> 10:19.676
 We'll see where we're at then.

10:19.678 --> 10:21.620
      (indistinct chatter)

10:22.697 --> 10:24.530
         Hi, I'm Serena.

10:24.607 --> 10:25.790
     This is Lily and Grace.

10:25.867 --> 10:27.125
            -Weet up.
              -Hyai.

10:27.276 --> 10:29.686
  Are you interested in pledging
       for Alpha Delta Pi?

10:29.688 --> 10:32.522
   Yeah! I hear you guys throw
      all the best parties.

10:32.524 --> 10:35.116
               ALL:
     Well, we've been waiting
       for you all summer,

10:35.193 --> 10:38.136
        and we're so glad
       you're finally here.

10:38.213 --> 10:41.222
     (all screaming happily)

10:42.701 --> 10:45.126
        GIRLS (chanting):
       Boom, boom, I wanna
           go A D Pi...

10:45.128 --> 10:46.536
              PETER:
          Meg, you gotta
       get me out of here.

10:46.538 --> 10:48.371
         These people are
       out of their minds.

10:48.373 --> 10:51.298
     Do not go A D Pi, Meg.
     Do not join this thing.

10:51.376 --> 10:53.559
      They don't let us out
           of the pile.

10:53.636 --> 10:56.321
      They're so mean, Meg.
         They're so mean.

10:56.323 --> 10:57.739
        SORORITY SISTERS:
        I wanna go A D Pi,
            don't you?

11:05.332 --> 11:09.075
   Hey, Meg, I'm a hippie now,
    and I'm feeling the burn.

11:09.152 --> 11:11.819
         -Bernie Sanders?
         -No, none of my
    hippie girlfriends shower,

11:11.897 --> 11:13.246
      and my crotch itches.

11:13.248 --> 11:15.248
      You know, despite what
        we're doing here,

11:15.324 --> 11:17.175
    -I'm still your daughter.
          -Right, right.

11:17.252 --> 11:18.343
     Hey, uh, would you sign
          this petition

11:18.345 --> 11:20.086
  to help save the spotted owl?

11:20.163 --> 11:21.829
           -Yeah, sure.
            -Awesome.

11:21.907 --> 11:23.682
   You're our 50th signature.

11:23.684 --> 11:25.425
      So what happens now?

11:25.427 --> 11:26.685
           Buck, wait!

11:26.761 --> 11:28.669
        -(chain saw revs)
              -Buck!

11:28.747 --> 11:31.189
     They got 50 signatures.

11:31.266 --> 11:32.432
      That's 50 all right.

11:32.508 --> 11:35.919
       Well, let's get back
          in the truck.

11:35.921 --> 11:38.196
               ♪

11:38.273 --> 11:41.533
        You don't have to
        be afraid anymore.

11:41.535 --> 11:43.184
        I'm still itchy.

11:43.261 --> 11:45.853
               MEG:
   Dad, I'm holding the ladder!

11:45.931 --> 11:48.998
               ♪

11:50.602 --> 11:53.712
    There he is, the big dog.
       You ready to sweat?

11:53.788 --> 11:56.122
    Today we got legs, and I'm
    gonna tell you everything

11:56.199 --> 11:57.774
  I've ever watched on Netflix.

11:57.776 --> 12:00.276
Stewie, listen, I don't want you
  to take this the wrong way,

12:00.278 --> 12:02.462
    but I got a new trainer.

12:02.538 --> 12:04.305
        New trainer? Who?

12:06.785 --> 12:08.451
           Doug? Ugh.

12:08.453 --> 12:11.804
      That's right, Stewie,
     it's an ugh-Doug moment.

12:11.881 --> 12:13.231
        No hard feelings.

12:13.308 --> 12:15.291
        I think Brian here
       just wants to rev up

12:15.293 --> 12:17.551
       -to a higher octane.
     -See you around, Stewie.

12:17.629 --> 12:21.406
   So it might take me a little
   longer to train you, Brian.

12:21.483 --> 12:24.391
 You're going to have to unlearn
  everything Stewie taught you.

12:24.393 --> 12:26.819
      Fortunately, that was
         almost nothing.

12:26.896 --> 12:28.321
         (Brian laughs)

12:28.397 --> 12:30.823
            Oh, man.

12:30.900 --> 12:33.001
               ♪

12:35.238 --> 12:36.254
              PETER:
            Heads up.

12:36.331 --> 12:40.149
     Ow! Dad, what the hell?

12:40.151 --> 12:41.484
      Did you join a frat?

12:41.486 --> 12:43.428
      I tried to, but I got
      the letters mixed up

12:43.505 --> 12:45.221
       and joined a fart.

12:46.433 --> 12:47.673
          (flatulence)

12:47.750 --> 12:49.342
            (laughs)

12:49.418 --> 12:53.087
  Hey, everyone, I'm in college,
    but here's a test for you.

12:53.164 --> 12:55.348
         We just gave you
      the easiest joke setup

12:55.424 --> 12:58.759
      in<i> Family Guy</i> history:
    Peter joins a fart house.

12:58.761 --> 13:00.695
   Is the correct punchline A?

13:02.765 --> 13:04.699
               B?

13:07.362 --> 13:09.329
              Or C?

13:12.608 --> 13:15.351
        Good luck to you.
    And now back to our story.

13:15.353 --> 13:19.280
 Hey, ladies, toga farty tonight
          at I Delta PU.

13:19.282 --> 13:21.132
       -Tell your friends.
             -Ew, no.

13:21.209 --> 13:23.192
     Heh, they all say that.

13:23.194 --> 13:25.286
   -Hey, what are you reading?
     -Boning up for an exam.

13:25.363 --> 13:28.047
   I boned up yesterday when
I walked into the girls' shower.

13:28.124 --> 13:29.198
  (classic slide whistle riff)

13:29.200 --> 13:30.533
          Dad,<i> please!</i>

13:30.552 --> 13:32.702
  Sorry, Meg, I've been smoking
       doobies all morning.

13:32.704 --> 13:34.720
  Talk about higher education.

13:34.722 --> 13:36.314
     (classic up-down slide)

13:36.391 --> 13:38.558
            That's it.
    I can't take this anymore.

13:38.634 --> 13:40.376
      Dad, get out of here.

13:40.378 --> 13:42.320
 What? This is what college is.

13:42.397 --> 13:44.823
         How do you know?
 You're not even a student here.

13:44.899 --> 13:46.399
      You're a total fraud.

13:46.401 --> 13:48.309
  Me? You wouldn't even be here

13:48.386 --> 13:49.327
   if your mother and I didn't

13:49.404 --> 13:51.329
   -pay someone to get you in.
             -What?!

13:51.406 --> 13:53.665
   Yeah, your whole application
            was fake.

13:53.667 --> 13:55.316
       Meg, is this true?

13:55.393 --> 13:58.561
     What? No, of course not,
           Dean Nearby.

13:58.563 --> 14:02.415
         Well, if it is,
  you're going to be suspended.

14:02.491 --> 14:03.675
             Oh, no.

14:03.677 --> 14:05.251
 Well, that weekend on the Cape

14:05.253 --> 14:07.595
     with Principal Shepherd
           was a waste.

14:11.500 --> 14:13.259
          I know I said
      I wouldn't get clingy,

14:13.336 --> 14:15.395
         but when can I
         see you again?

14:21.252 --> 14:23.586
         I can't believe
       they suspended Meg.

14:23.588 --> 14:27.198
 Suspended Meg? Peter, you and I
     could be going to jail.

14:27.200 --> 14:29.683
       I can't go to jail.
     Me and my fart brothers

14:29.761 --> 14:31.777
      are supposed to streak
         the quad later.

14:31.854 --> 14:33.187
      (plays "Charge" riff)

14:33.264 --> 14:35.114
          Now stop that.
          You're not in

14:35.191 --> 14:37.100
       whatever you think
       college is anymore.

14:37.102 --> 14:38.768
     I can't believe you two
         did this to me.

14:38.770 --> 14:40.361
  Maybe if you believed in me,

14:40.438 --> 14:42.213
     none of this would have
            happened.

14:42.290 --> 14:44.549
  Meg, honey, nobody wanted you
        out of this house

14:44.551 --> 14:45.625
        more than we did.

14:45.743 --> 14:47.126
  You know, maybe there's a way

14:47.203 --> 14:48.444
  none of you gets in trouble.

14:48.446 --> 14:49.721
   What are you talking about?

14:49.839 --> 14:51.222
    Well, you said you can do

14:51.299 --> 14:52.632
         all those things
       on your application.

14:52.634 --> 14:55.284
   If you show you actually can
         do those things,

14:55.286 --> 14:56.619
    you're all in the clear.

14:56.621 --> 14:57.787
   And then I can get back to

14:57.789 --> 14:59.138
  hustling drunk women upstairs

14:59.215 --> 15:00.456
      with Tobin and Squee.

15:00.458 --> 15:02.383
   Well, I better get to work,
              then.

15:02.460 --> 15:05.236
    But I seriously doubt that
  I'll be able to pull this off.

15:05.313 --> 15:07.572
          Hey, come on.
       Anything's possible.

15:07.574 --> 15:10.283
  Like when that Starbucks cup
  made it onto<i> Game of Thrones.</i>

15:10.318 --> 15:12.410
           This is it.
  Here it comes, here it comes.

15:12.487 --> 15:15.396
              -Hey!
          -Oh, my gosh.
         -That's so cool.

15:15.473 --> 15:18.082
      I can't believe this.
   What's the Internet saying?

15:18.084 --> 15:21.419
        They-they thought
         you were great.

15:24.315 --> 15:26.649
     Okay, Brian, this many.

15:26.651 --> 15:29.485
           -(straining)
           -This many.

15:29.487 --> 15:31.429
 Come on, Brian, you can do it.

15:31.506 --> 15:33.656
           (straining)

15:33.658 --> 15:37.584
  And that's as many as I know.
         Good job, Brian.

15:37.662 --> 15:40.163
           Hey, Stewie,
    congratulate your friend.

15:40.165 --> 15:42.423
 He just did this many sit-ups.

15:42.500 --> 15:44.350
      What? There's nothing
           after that.

15:44.427 --> 15:47.170
   -That's as high as it goes.
         -(chuckles) Yep.

15:47.172 --> 15:49.280
          Are you crazy,
      pushing him that hard?

15:49.357 --> 15:51.098
You're playing a dangerous game.

15:51.176 --> 15:53.176
      Yeah, it's dangerous.

15:53.178 --> 15:55.328
  And that's the way I like it.

16:02.295 --> 16:05.188
     Listen, Doug, I've been
     meaning to talk to you.

16:05.190 --> 16:08.708
     I just got this new job,
    and the commute is... ugh.

16:08.784 --> 16:10.284
        I can work around
          your schedule.

16:10.361 --> 16:12.545
     Well, that's the thing.
        I don't have one.

16:12.621 --> 16:15.122
     That's the way the suits
        figured it anyway.

16:15.200 --> 16:17.216
    What exactly is this job?

16:17.293 --> 16:19.126
          I know, right?
  Anyway, you've been terrific,

16:19.204 --> 16:20.461
   and I'm gonna keep at this.

16:20.538 --> 16:22.296
 But I'm afraid this is goodbye.

16:22.373 --> 16:24.089
       What if I went down
         to $300 a week?

16:24.167 --> 16:26.442
   -STEWIE: You're<i> paying</i> him?!
           -I'm sorry.

16:29.230 --> 16:30.488
       (blows raspberries)

16:30.490 --> 16:33.216
      Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa.
    There's no need for that.

16:33.218 --> 16:35.234
       (blows raspberries)

16:35.236 --> 16:37.811
   -Thank you for that, Brian.
     -You're welcome, Stewie.

16:37.889 --> 16:40.890
 You know, this whole thing has
 taught me an important lesson.

16:40.892 --> 16:42.667
        I hate exercise.

16:42.669 --> 16:44.076
            Gay-men.

16:44.153 --> 16:47.321
     Somebody has to help me
      walk down the stairs.

16:47.398 --> 16:49.298
               ♪

16:53.404 --> 16:56.180
     <i> MAN (through bullhorn):</i>
    <i> Everyone, if I could have</i>
         <i> your attention.</i>

16:56.257 --> 16:59.575
    <i> I'm Dean Distant Faraway,</i>
       <i> and we're here today</i>

16:59.577 --> 17:02.912
   <i> to determine whether or not</i>
     <i> Meg Griffin can justify</i>

17:02.914 --> 17:05.431
<i>her admission to our university.</i>

17:05.508 --> 17:07.674
   -And we're Mom and Dad. Hi.
            -Go blue.

17:07.676 --> 17:10.844
         <i> DISTANT FARAWAY:</i>
        <i> What did they say?</i>
       <i> I-I'm very far away.</i>

17:10.922 --> 17:13.364
               ♪

17:15.777 --> 17:17.777
             Strike.

17:17.853 --> 17:19.287
         (all cheering)

17:25.420 --> 17:27.295
         (all cheering)

17:32.794 --> 17:34.126
         (all cheering)

17:34.203 --> 17:36.554
        Ah... Dr. Nassar?

17:36.631 --> 17:40.433
     -(whispers indistinctly)
      -(gasps) Oh, my stars.

17:43.229 --> 17:46.655
   Okay, I'm gonna try to kill
  two birds with one stone here.

17:46.657 --> 17:48.457
         I'll be singing
     "Love is a Battlefield"

17:48.459 --> 17:51.069
         -by Pat Benatar.
           -(murmuring)

17:51.145 --> 17:52.719
           In Russian.

17:52.797 --> 17:54.238
        (excited chatter)

17:54.315 --> 17:56.482
             -Hit it.
         -(music starts)

17:57.635 --> 18:01.728
    ♪<i> Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,</i>
 <i> whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa</i> ♪

18:01.806 --> 18:03.998
         ♪<i> My sil'nyy</i> ♪

18:05.085 --> 18:07.827
 ♪<i> Nikito Nam Ne Skazhet chto</i> ♪

18:07.829 --> 18:10.904
         ♪<i> My ne pravy</i> ♪

18:10.982 --> 18:12.739
      ♪<i> Dolgo ishchen vy</i> ♪

18:12.741 --> 18:15.835
       ♪<i> Nashix serdtsa</i> ♪

18:15.911 --> 18:19.263
      ♪<i> My oba znaem chto</i> ♪

18:21.417 --> 18:25.419
   ♪<i> Lyubov eto battlefield.</i> ♪

18:25.496 --> 18:28.255
           (cheering)

18:28.333 --> 18:31.109
   Well, it appears you can do
      pretty much everything

18:31.111 --> 18:33.111
you claimed on your application.

18:33.187 --> 18:35.855
          So that's it?
       I'm back in school?

18:35.857 --> 18:37.281
 I think all you have to do now

18:37.358 --> 18:40.409
         is prove you can
 windsurf over Providence Falls.

18:43.439 --> 18:44.697
           Oh, right.

18:44.699 --> 18:46.791
  You prove that, you're back.

18:46.868 --> 18:49.702
 Wait, did we check that she can
    get dunked on by her dad?

18:49.704 --> 18:50.703
      Dunked on by my d...?

18:50.779 --> 18:52.713
               Oh!

18:53.858 --> 18:56.175
     You gotta get big, Meg.

19:01.716 --> 19:03.457
           (cheering)

19:03.534 --> 19:06.385
  Guys, no matter what happens,
     I just want you to know

19:06.462 --> 19:08.721
        that I forgive you
        for what you did.

19:08.797 --> 19:11.298
    I know deep down you were
    just looking out for me.

19:11.376 --> 19:13.467
       Whatever you think
       the lesson is here

19:13.469 --> 19:14.560
         is fine by us.

19:14.637 --> 19:16.821
         (fanfare plays)

19:16.898 --> 19:19.490
         Good luck, Meg.
           We love you.

19:19.567 --> 19:21.367
        (crowd cheering)

19:25.331 --> 19:27.331
               ♪

19:30.077 --> 19:32.295
        (breathes deeply)

19:37.326 --> 19:39.343
             Aah...

19:39.420 --> 19:41.737
          Aw, so close.

19:41.739 --> 19:43.088
        (crowd screaming)

19:43.165 --> 19:45.165
          (Meg yelling)

19:45.243 --> 19:46.667
    Peter, call an ambulance.

19:46.669 --> 19:49.687
          Can you do it?
   My number's blocked by 911.

20:18.200 --> 20:21.110
    Come on, you can do this.
    Stewie does it every day.

20:21.112 --> 20:22.445
            -He does?
              -Yep.

20:22.447 --> 20:23.971
 Just put one hand on the rail.

20:28.210 --> 20:29.785
        Damn it, I can't.

20:29.787 --> 20:31.562
             Uppies.

20:34.400 --> 20:36.292
          Adios, Doug.

20:36.294 --> 20:40.071
        From hell's heart
         I stab at thee.

20:40.147 --> 20:45.317
       With my last breath,
          I spit upon...

20:45.394 --> 20:47.286
            (snoring)

20:49.415 --> 20:51.249
        Ha! What a baby.